Subject: [PATCH] mac80211: initialize the host queue on the offload path

HAS_TX_QUEUE skips ieee80211_select_queue() but queue still indexes
vif.hw_queue and, for non-NSS hardware offload, station statistics.
Use a safe BE host queue before optional software classification. The
netdev queue mapping is a CPU flow-hash queue under NSS and must not be
used as an AC index. Firmware DSCP/TID classification is unchanged.

--- a/net/mac80211/tx.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/tx.c
@@ -4766,7 +4766,7 @@ static void ieee80211_8023_xmit(struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata,
 	struct tid_ampdu_tx *tid_tx = NULL;
 	struct sk_buff *seg, *next;
 	unsigned int skbs = 0, len = 0;
-	u16 queue;
+	u16 queue = IEEE80211_AC_BE;
 	u8 tid;
 
 	if (unlikely(!ieee80211_hw_check(&local->hw, HAS_TX_QUEUE))) {
